                        "form": "lazed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "64327274-fdb6-30b7-ab1f-631f906d5f25",
                        "entry_id": "03cbf2dd-c82f-39b0-b458-5ff7cb132910",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be lazy, waste time."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "245022e0-40b6-4803-8a3e-b0f4e0f3cf24",
                                "sense_id": "64327274-fdb6-30b7-ab1f-631f906d5f25",
                                "text": "Behold by millions how thy men do fall\nBefore Alphonsus like to sillie sheepe.\nAnd canst thou stand still lazing in this sort?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dab0124c-a193-4fe4-8c3f-f9a0647c71fa",
                                "sense_id": "64327274-fdb6-30b7-ab1f-631f906d5f25",
                                "text": "And, lastly, such are they; that, having got\nWealth, Knowledge, and those other Gifts, which may\nAdvance the Publike-Good, yet, use them not;\nBut Feede, and Sleepe, and laze their time away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e4309c1-efd4-4529-bfb5-2d1d4053c06f",
                                "sense_id": "64327274-fdb6-30b7-ab1f-631f906d5f25",
                                "text": "But for this anachronism of keeping Saturday holy when you had Sunday also to laze on, Daniel felt a hundred higher careers would have been open to him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94ddeddf-8797-4795-8153-01ba8c4df74a",
                                "sense_id": "64327274-fdb6-30b7-ab1f-631f906d5f25",
                                "text": "“I could easily fall into this,” I said. “Laze my way through life. Coffee here, wine there. You can channel significant things into the commonplace. Or you can avoid them completely.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f34f2b7-b6d2-377f-9282-ad12b3a1510e",
                        "entry_id": "03cbf2dd-c82f-39b0-b458-5ff7cb132910",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To pass time relaxing; to relax, lounge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f03bb0c-3788-467d-a450-2acc6d18deba",
                                "sense_id": "2f34f2b7-b6d2-377f-9282-ad12b3a1510e",
                                "text": "The cat spent the afternoon lazing in the sun."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fa3138d-1297-4389-a54d-74a7692b9bed",
                                "sense_id": "2f34f2b7-b6d2-377f-9282-ad12b3a1510e",
                                "text": "A football game went on beside the line; half the teams just lazed on the grass […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
